ole": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "The neighbourhood_evolution probe (step_01) shows a pronounced peak change (~0.302) centered at t=13963 using the 5000-unit half-window, indicating an abrupt shift in the group's contact set. Individual nodes exhibit clear before/after partner differences: e.g. node 1039 had 30 neighbors before and 0 after (steps 06\u201307), 1119 went from 31 to 2 neighbors (steps 10\u201311), while 1389 shows the reverse (steps 08\u201309). Several other group members similarly gain or lose many partners across the same boundary (steps 12\u201315). I controlled for alternative explanations: overall activity dropped between the two half-windows (steps 02\u201303) and top-active-node lists changed (steps 04\u201305), which could partially influence partner counts, but the concentrated, simultaneous turnover in partner identities around the same time is consistent with an abrupt regime switch rather than slow background drift."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8b4a3bfa\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"t